WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.570
- [Narrator] Thanks to CuriosityStream

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:03.523
for keeping Legal Eagle in the air.

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.770
- Hello, did somebody say "lawyer?"

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.440
Richard A. Bottomfeeder, attorney at law.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:09.540
- I take exception to that.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.470
Lawyers are not bottom feeders,

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.921
even when they are literal
bottom-feeding fish.

00:00:13.921 --> 00:00:16.588
(playful music)

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.070
Hey legal eagles, it's time
to think like a lawyer,

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.360
and today we are covering
the highly-requested

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.890
episode of SpongeBob Squarepants,
Krabs versus Plankton.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.780
This will probably be the last cartoon

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.470
I cover for a while, you
can check out my breakdowns

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.600
of The Simpsons and South Park

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.500
down in the description below.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.770
I thought it would be fun to end

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.420
with an example of maritime law,

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.232
and SpongeBob Squarepants
technically qualifies.

00:00:41.232 --> 00:00:43.030
(buzzer buzzes)
- I surrender!

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:45.060
- Be sure to comment in
the form of an objection,

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.360
which I'll either sustain or overrule,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.950
and stick around until
the end of the video

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.690
where I give SpongeBob Squarepants

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.630
a grade for legal realism.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.450
So without further ado, let's dig in

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.990
to this episode of SpongeBob Squarepants,

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.789
Krabs versus Plankton.

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:02.010
(playful music)

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.670
Okay so Plankton is
going to the Krusty Krab

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:08.280
in order to steal the recipe
for the Krusty Burger.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.120
Wait, no no no, that's The Simpsons.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:10.953
- D'oh!

00:01:10.953 --> 00:01:12.760
- He's going to steal the
recipe for the Krabby Patty,

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.350
okay, that's it, the Krabby Patty,

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.250
which is probably some
sort of trade secret

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.940
in the same way that
Kentucky Fried Chicken

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:21.140
is a trade secret or Coca
Cola is a trade secret,

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.610
but I'm guessing Plankton
probably does this

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.430
on more than one occasion,
kinda like Wile E. Coyote.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.977
- That was easy, maybe today is the day

00:01:28.977 --> 00:01:33.977
I'm gonna steal the Krabby
Patty formula. (grunts)

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.420
- All right, a classic slip and fall case.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.730
There is an entire genre of lawsuits

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.530
devoted to exactly this kind of thing,

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:43.820
this kind of personal injury,

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.760
because it's so easy to fake
your injuries like this.

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.857
So this is the kind of
thing that gives lawyers

00:01:48.857 --> 00:01:50.906
and lawsuits a bad name.

00:01:50.906 --> 00:01:53.310
- Look at you, Plankton, once again

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.190
you've fallen flat on your back

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:58.220
in another pathetic attempt
to steal me formula.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:00.079
Though you tried and tried,

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:03.116
you haven't had the smallest nibble

00:02:03.116 --> 00:02:07.300
of my delicious formula,
and you never will! (laughs)

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.520
- I mean, the guy has
already injured himself,

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.940
there's no reason to be
mean to him and taunt him

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.240
when he's on the ground.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:16.760
Not a good idea for a restaurant
owner to be that malicious.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:17.990
- How do you sleep at night

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.090
knowing you're a complete
failure? (laughs)

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.620
- There really should be a wet floor sign.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.830
- Yeah, if that were me who slipped,

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.810
I'd sue Old Man Krabs for all he's got.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:30.910
- You know, that's a very good point.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:35.260
There probably should be a
wet floor sign in the vicinity

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.120
when someone is mopping up the floor,

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.210
although I query how
you can mop up a floor

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:41.840
and have standing water when you're

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.960
literally under water in the first place.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.780
Putting that aside for the moment,

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:48.650
I think these patrons
are absolutely right,

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:53.070
that there should be a wet
floor sign in the vicinity.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.860
- Does that include the
Krabby Patty formula?

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:56.793
- Of course.

00:02:56.793 --> 00:02:59.196
(pensive music)
(laughs)

00:02:59.196 --> 00:03:00.807
- Oh the pain!

00:03:00.807 --> 00:03:03.488
I can't feel my arms and legs,

00:03:03.488 --> 00:03:05.238
I think they're broken.

00:03:05.238 --> 00:03:07.315
- Do plankton have arms and legs?

00:03:07.315 --> 00:03:08.700
- I'll sue for my pain and suffering.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:09.801
- Sue?

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:10.842
- Oh, that looks bad.

00:03:10.842 --> 00:03:11.950
- Uh-oh.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:12.850
- Poor little man.

00:03:16.323 --> 00:03:17.156
- Hold up a second.

00:03:17.156 --> 00:03:19.280
Plankton, we don't need to drag this

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.010
little incident into court, do we?

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:25.090
- Well, if you transfer the
Krabby Patty formula to me,

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:27.290
I'll forget your gross negligence.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.490
- Scoundrel, you'll have my formula

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:32.225
when you pry it from me lifeless claws.

00:03:32.225 --> 00:03:33.310
(Plankton laughs)

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.270
- Yeah, so this is actually based off of

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.940
the real-life case of
Whelan versus Van Natta,

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.950
where someone went to a shop legally,

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.020
but then snuck around
in a private residence

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.750
that was attached to the shop.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.970
The issue at hand is a question of being

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.130
an invitee versus a trespasser.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:51.810
An invitee is someone that is there

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:53.210
for regular business purposes,

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.420
and a trespasser is
someone who does not have

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.330
permission to be on the premises,

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:00.970
and generally speaking,
a landowner must act

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.700
as a reasonable person
would toward invitees,

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.990
and to figure out what a
reasonable person would do,

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:09.700
you look towards others who
are in exactly the same place.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.360
Given that we see wet floor
signs just about everywhere,

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.400
you can bet a reasonable restaurant owner

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.330
would probably put one out if
they were mopping the floor,

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.580
or they probably wouldn't
leave standing water

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.920
in your restaurant in the first place

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:23.710
where people can trip and fall.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.660
Now with respect to trespassers though,

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.680
a restaurant owner or
a landowner doesn't owe

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.300
the same duty of care.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.220
Basically if someone is
trespassing on your property,

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.150
your only obligation is to not hide

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.870
dangerous things or create
dangerous situations

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:40.020
on the premises, like the guy who created

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.700
a shotgun booby trap to punish people

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.695
who were breaking into his house.

00:04:44.695 --> 00:04:47.100
(evil laughing)

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.770
You know, what's really
interesting about this

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:51.250
particular case is that
California did away

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.480
with that invitee trespasser distinction

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.840
and replaced it with a sort of general

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.480
reasonable person standard.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.680
In the case of Rowland verus Christian,

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.630
the invitee trespasser
distinction was found

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:06.010
to be unhelpful by the court
and the court just held that

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:09.140
the landowner owes a duty
to act as a reasonable man,

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.840
now a reasonable person,
in sort of general.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.860
So it doesn't really
matter what the status

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.450
of the person who was
injured on the property is,

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.900
you just always have to
act as a reasonable person.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:22.100
Mr. Krabs has not put out the sign

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.950
that says there's a wet floor,

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:27.620
and so he's probably liable
under the California standard.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:29.787
- See you in court, Krabs.

00:05:29.787 --> 00:05:34.787
I'm mean, oh the pain,
the deep, frying pain.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.210
- Now of course, Plankton
is malingering here

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:41.040
and he's faking all of his injuries,

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.940
so that sort of shows you
that he hasn't actually

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.560
suffered any damages here
in this particular case,

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.800
and he's really perpetrating a fraud

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.270
on both Krabs and the court.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:52.820
But sometimes you can have a court case

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:55.530
where you're entitled to
one dollar in damages,

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:58.480
because I think Krabs may
have been in the wrong

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:02.159
to not have a sign out with
respect to everybody else,

00:06:02.159 --> 00:06:06.040
and so Plankton fell, he
just didn't really have

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:08.000
much damage as a result of that,

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.350
so he might be entitled to what are called

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:11.680
nominal damages and a jury might end up

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.990
awarding him one dollar instead of the

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:16.950
billions and the recipe
that he's actually seeking.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:20.060
- I'm in a blue ruin, I'm doomed.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:23.110
- Don't worry, Mr. Krabs,
I will do whatever it takes

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.230
to keep the Krusty Krab
formula from getting

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.300
into Plankton's evil hands.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.580
- What I really need is a good lawyer.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.120
- Hello, did somebody say "lawyer?"

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.800
Richard A. Bottomfeeder, attorney at law.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:34.880
- I take exception to that.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:36.810
Lawyers are not bottom feeders,

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:39.180
even when they are literal
bottom-feeding fish.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:42.230
- I couldn't help but notice
that despicable display.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:44.530
- So uh, how much is this gonna cost me?

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:47.345
- Actually, I won't charge
a dime unless we win.

00:06:47.345 --> 00:06:48.490
(cash register clinks)

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:51.090
- Yeah, that's a pretty
standard thing for a plaintiff's

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:54.030
attorney to charge, especially
in a personal injury lawsuit

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:57.080
because of the risk
and generally speaking,

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.620
if you're a plaintiff in
a personal injury case,

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.300
you probably don't have the fees

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:05.670
to pay someone hundreds of
dollars an hour to represent you,

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:07.760
so a plaintiff's lawyer in
this particular situation

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.900
would probably ask for
somewhere in the neighborhood

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.540
of 35 to 50% of any recovery.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:13.860
While it sounds like a lot,

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:15.840
the lawyer is actually
in a precarious position

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.480
where number one, the lawyer
might not recover anything,

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.500
and number two, the lawyer has to front

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.450
a lot of the court fees and
court costs that go along

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:25.400
with a lawsuit, which can
add up pretty quickly.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:28.020
- In fact, I think we should counter sue

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:29.937
for everything Plankton owns.

00:07:29.937 --> 00:07:31.470
(cash register clinks)

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.480
- That, so that is kind of a real thing.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.570
You are allowed to counter sue.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:39.340
Generally, what people do is they file

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:41.120
what are called compulsory counterclaims,

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:43.670
so they are things that
arise from the same

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:46.370
set of facts, and here
Krabs doesn't really have

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:47.870
any compulsory counterclaims,

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.800
there's nothing that must be brought

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.260
at the same time that
results from the same

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:55.070
nexus of facts that the
lawsuit arises from.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.350
The opposite of that is a
permissive counterclaim,

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:59.350
which you can bring in the same action

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:00.640
or you can bring it whenever you want,

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:02.750
because it doesn't really
relate to the claim at hand,

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.470
and that's what this lawyer
is asking to bring in,

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:07.820
is whatever past deeds have happened.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:09.770
There is some efficiency
gained because you're already

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:12.710
hashing out this claim
against the same party,

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.750
but courts don't really like
permissive counterclaims,

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:16.610
because it really multiplies
the number of things

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.170
that they have to deal with.

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:21.440
(SpongeBob hums)

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:22.273
- [SpongeBob] Mr. Krabs?

00:08:22.273 --> 00:08:23.106
- What is it, lad?

00:08:23.106 --> 00:08:24.870
- I thought you might
want to hear my testimony

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.770
for when you call me
as a character witness.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.170
I've been rehearsing it.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:30.390
- Actually SpongeBob, we won't be needing

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:31.650
any testimony from you.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.655
Why you'll be more of a uh,

00:08:33.655 --> 00:08:34.580
(whispering)

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.810
of a liability than an asset.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.090
- Yeah, and also you wouldn't
really have a character

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:41.753
witness in a slip and fall
case like this anyway.

00:08:41.753 --> 00:08:43.980
Character witness has no bearing on

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:46.650
whether negligence has occurred here,

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:47.580
whether there was a duty,

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:49.380
whether it was a breach of that duty,

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:52.140
it just, there's no reason
you would complicate things,

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.610
and it's a good idea not to call

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.710
SpongeBob Squarepants to the stand.

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:56.543
- But I--

00:08:56.543 --> 00:08:58.100
- Now run along, make things ship shape

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.880
for my victory celebration.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.530
I've gotta get to the courthouse early,

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:03.563
there's only a few free parking places.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:07.152
- Oh this is gonna be a slam dunk.

00:09:07.152 --> 00:09:08.235
(yelling)

00:09:08.235 --> 00:09:09.140
- Oh no!

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:11.710
Mr. Krabs's lawyer, speak to me.

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:14.040
- Wracked with pain.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.580
- So, sometimes this does actually happen.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:18.450
Sometimes the lead trial
counsel is rendered

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:21.250
incapacitated and you have to
pick up with somebody else.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:24.110
In fact, when I interviewed
my friend Brent Wisner,

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:26.840
who was the lead trial
counsel in the Monsanto

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:29.780
Round Up cases, the
original lead trial counsel

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.630
who was slated to handle everything

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.200
was injured in a wind surfing accident

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.900
just weeks before trial,
so he had to pick up

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:39.420
on the eve of trial and hand
out the whole thing himself

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.920
before he got a $2 billion verdict,

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:44.289
so it does happen from time to time.

00:09:44.289 --> 00:09:46.789
(tense music)

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:52.150
- I'll give you one last chance.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:55.990
I'll drop the charges if
you give me the formula.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.679
- Never, you little whelp!

00:09:57.679 --> 00:09:58.926
(audience gasps)

00:09:58.926 --> 00:10:02.520
- Ow, ow, my wittle arms.
(audience gasps)

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:06.020
- What, no, I didn't lay a claw on him.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:10.000
- Ow, my other arm, ow.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.310
- He's lying!

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.070
- I will say this is a little ridiculous.

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:14.730
It doesn't make any
sense that Plankton would

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:17.550
actually fight Krabs,
I don't think plankton

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.220
actually even have arms,

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:21.860
and I don't even think
crabs and plankton interact

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:23.590
with each other in the ocean anyway.

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:25.410
If only there were a biologist that could

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:28.719
rank these animals on some sort of a tier.

00:10:28.719 --> 00:10:31.052
(twinkling)

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.120
- [Narrator] Ocean-dwelling
crabs and zooplankton

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.970
interact quite frequently
in the reef meta.

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:38.600
SpongeBob's Plankton is most likely based

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:41.110
on the species of plankton
called the copepod,

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:43.270
a microscopic animal
that's actually in the same

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:46.570
sub-phylum as Mr. Krabs, since
they're both crustaceans.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:48.940
Similar to how those battles
are depicted in the show,

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:51.120
one on one it's really no contest.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:53.070
Crab builds that use the
filter feeding ability

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:55.190
actually directly target plankton mains

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:57.070
as their main source of XP.

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:58.460
So yeah, as it turns out,

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.880
SpongeBob's depiction
of the one-sided rivalry

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:02.800
between Mr. Krabs and Plankton

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.290
is actually fairly reasonable.

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:05.840
If you're interested in what the tier list

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:08.670
for the rest of the Bikini
Bottom residents looks like,

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:11.700
be sure to check out my
channel after you're done here.

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:13.890
- Huh, well that's good
to know, thanks TierZoo.

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:15.220
Now let's get back to the trial.

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:17.220
- Mr. Krabs, where is your attorney?

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:20.025
- I don't know where he could be.

00:11:20.025 --> 00:11:21.272
(door slams)
(crowd gasps)

00:11:21.272 --> 00:11:22.540
- Here I am.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.600
- Thank you for joining us, Mr.?

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.763
- SpongeBob Lawyerpants, your Honor.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:30.540
- Yeah, that is the
unauthorized practice of law.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.030
You are not allowed to
represent other people

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:35.850
if you have not gone to law
school and passed the bar,

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:38.320
and SpongeBob would face
serious repercussions

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.700
from pretending to be a lawyer right now.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.980
- What are you doing here, SpongeBob?

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:46.210
- Your lawyer uh, fell down on the job,

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:47.600
but don't worry Mr. Krabs,

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:51.226
I have everything under
control, it's all in here.

00:11:51.226 --> 00:11:52.059
- Really?

00:11:52.059 --> 00:11:52.892
- Yup, right--

00:11:52.892 --> 00:11:54.200
- Yeah, that's not gonna end well.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.670
- Is there a problem?

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:58.650
- Uh, your lawyer didn't
give me the combination.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:01.095
- Is the plaintiff ready to proceed?

00:12:01.095 --> 00:12:06.095
- Yes, your Honor, I'll try, ow, ow, ow.

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:10.250
- Although it's very
sympathetic, I really would not

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.450
counsel Plankton to
represent himself here,

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:14.710
he would do much better
to have an actual lawyer

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:17.720
to represent him instead of
doing everything on his own.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:20.440
That doesn't tend to end well for people.

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:24.700
- I wasn't always the
tortured shell of a protozoa

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:28.080
that writhes in pain before you today.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.810
I (groans) was a vibrant, carefree,

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:34.962
happy-go-lucky single cell.

00:12:34.962 --> 00:12:37.380
(dramatic music)

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:38.920
- Pull yourself together, boy.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:43.620
- Then came the fateful day
that I paid an innocent visit

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:47.680
to the death trap known
as the Krusty Krab.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:49.130
- Not a bad opening statement so far,

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:50.610
I kinda like it, very persuasive,

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:53.400
and definitely hits on
some good emotional beats.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:55.940
- Upon entering said establishment,

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:58.419
I found myself without any warning

00:12:58.419 --> 00:13:02.280
slipping and finally falling onto a hard,

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:05.826
unforgiving floor that
had been intentionally

00:13:05.826 --> 00:13:08.613
covered with a viscous fluid.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:11.620
- You know, he's a little
bit over the top here

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:12.620
in this opening statement.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.270
It doesn't actually matter
if Krabs intentionally

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.400
put the water there or not,

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.280
certainly if he did
intentionally put the water

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:19.520
and tried to hurt some people,

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:22.740
then that would be far
more than actual negligence

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.040
and that would border
on an intentional tort,

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.960
but just the fact that he was careless

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:30.180
and did not do what a normal
restaurant owner would do

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:32.280
would be enough to be guilty,

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:35.020
in this case liable for negligence.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:36.280
- Where was I?

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:39.789
Oh yeah, but the worst part is

00:13:39.789 --> 00:13:44.050
my dreams of completing a
marathon like I promised

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:48.163
my old Grammy have been dashed. (cries)

00:13:49.376 --> 00:13:52.397
I'm sorry, Gram Gram, I'm sorry.

00:13:53.485 --> 00:13:55.970
(crying)

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:58.483
Thank you for your kind attention.

00:13:59.658 --> 00:14:00.491
Suckers.

00:14:00.491 --> 00:14:03.160
- Does the defense (sniffles)
have an opening statement?

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.846
- Yes, your Honor.

00:14:04.846 --> 00:14:06.870
Poor Gram Gram!

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:08.020
- I probably don't need to tell you

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:10.130
that that is a terrible opening statement

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:11.870
and they would have done better to reserve

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.040
their opening statement and give it

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:14.350
at the start of their case in chief

00:14:14.350 --> 00:14:15.900
after the plaintiff has already gone.

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:18.130
Yeah, so far SpongeBob
not doing a good job.

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:20.080
And by the way, it shows how important

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.700
preparation is before the trial itself.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:24.928
They've done no discovery whatsoever,

00:14:24.928 --> 00:14:26.820
they just went straight into trial,

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:29.260
they haven't been able
to open the briefcase

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:31.190
that contains their entire defense.

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:34.320
- Mr. Krabs, can you identify this item?

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:36.430
- [Krabs] It's a wet floor sign.

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:37.720
- Do you own one?

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:41.971
- Uh, well, um, no, I don't.

00:14:41.971 --> 00:14:44.120
(dramatic music)
(jury gasps)

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:45.960
- I gotta hand it to Plankton,

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:49.760
that's a great question to
ask on cross examination.

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:51.807
Assuming that Plankton knows that

00:14:51.807 --> 00:14:55.050
Krabs does not in fact
own one of these signs,

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:57.060
that is probative to the case at hand,

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:59.444
it helps demonstrate his negligence

00:14:59.444 --> 00:15:02.060
by the fact that he doesn't own the sign,

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:02.950
he couldn't put it out

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:06.100
and the sign potentially
would have prevented

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:08.570
his injury in this particular case.

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:12.210
Good cross examination,
well done. (laughs)

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:13.730
- No, no, you don't understand.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:15.690
I had to make some
tough business decisions

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:18.580
and the sign seemed superfluous.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:20.817
- Yeah, I don't think that matters.

00:15:20.817 --> 00:15:21.840
(jury murmurs)

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:23.280
- No more questions.

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:26.160
- [Judge] Your witness, Mr. Lawyerpants.

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:28.020
- Yeah I don't know if
Plankton should have

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:29.280
stopped the cross examination there.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.800
He could have gotten
some other good points,

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:33.530
but I also don't think Krabs's defense

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:36.550
that he doesn't have
the money for the sign

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:38.014
would hold any water.

00:15:38.014 --> 00:15:39.310
(laughing)

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:43.066
Here, if you're not financially able

00:15:43.066 --> 00:15:46.180
to have a sign that is sort of necessary

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:48.810
for all restaurants and stores to have,

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:51.110
odds are you probably
shouldn't be in business,

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:52.960
so I don't think that's a good defense,

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:54.210
the fact that he did not own

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.500
and did not put out this wet floor sign.

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:59.330
- May it please the court,
ladies and gentlemen of the jury,

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:02.280
my client has been called cheap, miserly,

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:04.131
and chronically tight-fisted.

00:16:04.131 --> 00:16:05.370
- Uh.

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:07.190
- This is not relevant and not helpful.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:10.180
- As cheap as the
prosecution claims he is,

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:12.810
would he be able to sit there quietly

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:16.338
while I took out a dollar and
dropped it in the blender?

00:16:16.338 --> 00:16:17.774
(gasps)

00:16:17.774 --> 00:16:19.328
(blender whirs)

00:16:19.328 --> 00:16:20.411
- No, no, no!

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:22.600
- Oh boy.

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:25.323
- Daddy's got you, daddy's
got you, daddy's here.

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:27.900
- Yeah so in addition to showing that

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:30.240
SpongeBob did no preparation in terms of

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:32.750
preparing his witness and defendant

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:35.130
for actually taking the stand here,

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:37.370
he's also asking questions
that are in no way

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:38.780
relevant to the case at hand.

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:41.560
Whether or not Krabs is cheap in general

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:44.570
does nothing to address the fact of

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:47.690
whether he committed a negligent
act in the first place,

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:50.420
except to the extent that
Plankton has already done

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:53.640
to show that Krabs didn't own a sign

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:55.010
and therefore he couldn't put it out,

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:57.020
which definitely does go to negligence,

00:16:57.020 --> 00:16:59.950
so SpongeBob not doing a great job here.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:02.610
He's arguing against his own client.

00:17:02.610 --> 00:17:04.770
- Does the defense have
any witness to call?

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:09.207
- Yes, your Honor, defense
calls Squidward to the stand.

00:17:09.207 --> 00:17:12.560
- Ah, Squidward, a loyal employee.

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:16.820
- Mr. Squidward, is it, my
client has been called cheap.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:19.430
Would you agree with
that ludicrous statement?

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:20.263
- Yes.

00:17:20.263 --> 00:17:22.430
- You know, again, this has no relevance,

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:25.310
and the last thing you want
to do is try to show character

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.780
here when it's not relevant
to the case at hand.

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:29.844
- Can you tell the court of some instance

00:17:29.844 --> 00:17:32.720
of Mr. Krabs's generosity in any way?

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:34.150
- Nope, can I go now?

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:35.839
- Generosity not relevant.

00:17:35.839 --> 00:17:39.660
- So it was you who made the
floor slippery, wasn't it?

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.180
Answer the question!

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:44.683
Need I remind you that
you, sir, are under oath?

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:47.130
- I don't know how you
put a mop under oath,

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:49.440
but yeah, he would be under oath.

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:52.210
- It's, it's just his lunch.

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.843
Or is it?

00:17:55.393 --> 00:17:57.332
(twinkling)

00:17:57.332 --> 00:18:00.181
- Defense calls Plankton to the stand.

00:18:00.181 --> 00:18:01.023
(dramatic music)

00:18:01.023 --> 00:18:04.750
Why did you go into the
Krusty Krab that day?

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:06.370
- Ah, that's a really good question.

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:07.950
That would definitely help his case

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:11.820
if Plankton actually
answers truthfully here.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.840
- To you know, say hello

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.870
to my once good friend Mr. Krabs, what?

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:20.897
- Are you sure it wasn't to
make off with one of these?

00:18:20.897 --> 00:18:23.757
- Aha, getting to the heart of the matter.

00:18:23.757 --> 00:18:25.240
- Gotcha.

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:28.220
Weren't you there to steal the formula

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:31.370
of the most delicious,
sweet-smelling sandwich

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:33.183
known to Bikini Bottom?

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:35.593
Krabby Patty.

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:40.273
(groaning nervously)

00:18:46.949 --> 00:18:49.095
- I can't take it!

00:18:49.095 --> 00:18:51.853
Gimme, gimme, gimme, gimme.

00:18:51.853 --> 00:18:53.700
Yippee! (laughing)

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:55.430
- Well, he didn't really
answer the question,

00:18:55.430 --> 00:18:58.690
but he did show that he was
faking all of his injuries,

00:18:58.690 --> 00:19:00.320
which probably is not going to be good

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.580
for his particular case.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:03.940
But interestingly, as we established,

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:05.910
putting aside the fact
that Plankton totally faked

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:09.060
all of his injuries,
depends on the jurisdiction.

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:12.320
If they were in California,
I think arguably

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:14.200
Krabs was probably in the wrong.

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:15.826
If we're in most states, however,

00:19:15.826 --> 00:19:18.540
Plankton was in the wrong
because he was a trespasser

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:19.770
and not an invitee.

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:21.740
- Has the jury reached a verdict?

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:23.040
- We have, your Honor.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:26.330
We find the defendant not guilty.

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:27.163
- Uh.

00:19:27.163 --> 00:19:28.500
- But he is cheap.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.280
- So this is a civil case.

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:32.890
Civil cases don't decide
guilt or innocence,

00:19:32.890 --> 00:19:35.540
civil cases decide
damages want who's liable

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:38.210
and who's not liable, so uh, (laughs)

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:41.300
the jury would not decide
that Krabs was not guilty,

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:44.690
they would decide that he was
not liable, owed no damages.

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:45.523
- I made you a present.

00:19:45.523 --> 00:19:48.187
- A present for me?

00:19:48.187 --> 00:19:51.033
- Close your eyes and hold out your hand.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:54.730
(groans)

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:57.500
It's a wet floor sign, I made it myself.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:59.338
- Well, it'll do.

00:19:59.338 --> 00:20:01.845
- It's better than nothing, I guess.

00:20:01.845 --> 00:20:04.512
(playful music)

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.500
Okay so now it's time to give this episode

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:10.891
of SpongeBob Squarepants
a grade for legal realism.

00:20:10.891 --> 00:20:13.100
(gavel bangs)

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:15.420
On the one hand, you
have a really interesting

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:17.410
fact pattern that is clearly based on

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:20.770
real-life cases and deals with real issues

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:23.190
like the standard of care
that is owed to people

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:25.140
that are on your property,
whether someone is

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:27.160
an invitee versus a trespasser.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:30.360
On the other hand, you have
some unauthorized practice

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:32.710
of law, you have an
abbreviated time period,

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:35.680
and you have some ridiculous
inter-species fighting

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:37.090
and fraud on the courts.

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.120
But all in all, I'm pleasantly surprised

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:40.870
at how much realism they
were able to squeeze in

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:43.750
to 10 minutes, so I'm
gonna give this episode

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.510
of SpongeBob Squarepants a C+,

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:49.510
specifically a pineapple under the sea.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:52.490
- I am now going to assault your mind

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:53.953
with subliminal messages.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:56.210
- Now this is not the first time

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:57.990
that TierZoo and I have teamed up.

00:20:57.990 --> 00:21:00.220
In fact, we actually
helped build a platform

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:02.190
for creators so they
don't have to worry about

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:03.640
things like demonetization.

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:04.620
It's called Nebula,

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:07.300
and we're partnering with CuriosityStream.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:09.460
As you may know, some friends
and I recently launched

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:11.680
our own streaming service called Nebula,

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:16.040
featuring lots of YouTube's
top educational-ish creators,

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:18.030
including Polyphonic, Knowing Better,

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:21.917
Wendover, Lindsay Ellis,
12tone, and of course TierZoo.

00:21:21.917 --> 00:21:24.490
We get the freedom to create
and we never have to worry

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:26.400
about the dreaded algorithm.

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:28.450
TierZoo and I are
actually competing to see

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:29.740
who can get more sign-ups.

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:31.811
Please don't make me look
bad in front of TierZoo.

00:21:31.811 --> 00:21:33.912
(imitating punching)

00:21:33.912 --> 00:21:34.880
(knuckles popping)

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:37.270
But seriously, we put a
lot of work into this.

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:39.170
We are really proud of the result.

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:40.640
It's a place where creators can

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:42.700
do what they do best, create.

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:45.350
It's a place where we can
both house content ad free

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:47.710
and also experiment with
new, original series

00:21:47.710 --> 00:21:49.840
that probably wouldn't
have worked on YouTube,

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:52.250
including an exclusive
series called Working Titles,

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:54.930
where every episode a
different creator breaks down

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:57.000
their favorite TV intro sequence.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.620
Polyphonic did Game of Thrones,

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:00.200
Patrick Willems did X-Men,

00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:02.795
and I'll be covering
Law &amp; Order very soon.

00:22:02.795 --> 00:22:04.290
(gavel bangs)

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:06.600
So what does this have to
do with CuriosityStream?

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:09.320
Well, they love educational
content and educational

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:12.640
creators, so they are the
perfect partner for Nebula.

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:14.270
We recently just worked out a deal

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:16.410
